# AWS S3 File Copy Automation Using Lambda and DynamoDB

## 1. Project Overview

This project automates file transfers between two Amazon S3 buckets using AWS Lambda. When a file is uploaded to the public S3 bucket, an S3 event automatically triggers the Lambda function. The function copies the uploaded object to a private S3 bucket and records the transfer details in a DynamoDB table.

The solution improves file-transfer automation, logging, and visibility into the movement of files between buckets.

## 2. Objectives

- Create a public S3 bucket for file uploads.
- Create a private S3 bucket for secure storage.
- Configure an AWS Lambda function to copy uploaded objects automatically.
- Create an IAM execution role and attach the required permissions.
- Store file-copy logs in DynamoDB.
- Test the workflow using `sample.zip`.
- Verify the copied object and corresponding database log.

